Woo! After playing Nethack since around 1986 and never having ascended
a character until my Valkyrie last year (http://www.cuse.org/goofy/
first_nethack_win.png) I've now ascended a Rogue. You can see a big
screengrab of the ending here -- http://www.cuse.org/nethack_win2.png
-- except I accidentally skipped the creatures killed and intrinsics
screens. Fortunately I had the latter written down in notepad anyway
from using a wand of enlightenment right before the ascension run, so
I'll paste it below.

Some highlights from the trip:

Krayus started out with 15 +1 daggers, and spent much of the early
game throwing them so as to reach expert in dagger AND inflict max
damage as often as possible. His god Kos got angry with him when he
was level six because he prayed too early, which he then promptly made
worse by kicking an altar while trying to clear stuff off from on top
of it. Whoops! So there was no praying possible from levels 6 to 12,
when monsters finally started getting generated that could mollify the
angry god.

He found a pair of Gauntlets of Power in minetown, and shortly
thereafter got a lucky polymorph trap that kept him human but bumped
him from level 12 to 14. Sokoban yielded a bag of holding, and two
levels later a random spawn gave an "reflection, which he wore until
getting the shield from Medusa. During his adventures he found  and
raided Fort Ludios (first time ever), and obtained not one but TWO
wishes from a single throne (in only three sits) on Dlvl 12. These
yielded a blessed +2 GDSM and a blessed fixed +2 oilskin cloak.
Arriving at Medusa's, he had no means of levitation, so he had to
wander for a time looking for rings.

During this time, he paid for five points of protection and then
promptly lost it all due to stupidly praying too early. Again. He
would eventually buy four more points. He also did the Rogue's Quest
while at levels 18 and 19, and afterwards spent a lot of time
sacrificing (earning Stormbringer, and visits from Juiblex and
Yeenoguh). He also genocided all Liches, humanoids, Rust Monsters and
Disenchanters. Finally he gave up trying to find a =levitation and
polypiled for it, also gaining =polymorph control, =teleport control,
a magic marker, and =conflict.

Getting past Medusa, he found himself at the castle, which he stormed.
The /wishing there gave him 2 blessed ?charging, a blessed amulet of
life saving (safety first!), 3 blessed ?enchant armor that he used to
improve his crappy AC, and two attempts at Magicbane, both of which
failed. Fortunately he had the rest of the armor he would need for
ascension at this point from random drops (speed boots, t-shirt, elven
leather helm), so he didn't have to use wishes on those.

He entered the VoD and wraith-danced his way to level 30 by luring
them down to Gehennom. From there he explored the mazes (unlike some,
Krayus enjoys mapping out every level of Gehennom in its entirety). He
killed Asmodeus, Baal, Geryon, and Orcus, finding another /Wishing in
Orcus Town, which this time successfully yielded a blessed Fixed +2
MagicBane, which he enchanted to +5 and used for the rest of the game.
He killed Vlad with a rusty pickaxe (renamed ValdsBane of course), and
was gifted a genocide from Vlad's throne, which he used on Green
Slimes because they annoyed him. He found the Vibrating Square on Dlvl
49, and proceeded to gear up for the Ascension Run.

Things went pretty quickly from there - the mysterious force was
relatively kind, and while Rodney showed up several times and even
managed to steal the Amulet of Yendor once, he died under MagicBane's
assault numerous times (I think about eight). The Elemental Planes
were speedy thanks to stocking up on scrolls of gold detection and
potions of booze, though the Air Elementals did a surprising amount of
damage to a well-armored Krayus. He still arrived on the Astral Plane
in good health, however. This was fortunate, since he was about to
have an experience of incredible stupidity.

The first altar that Krayus got to, fighting his way through Death and
the hordes around him with help from a =conflict, was the correct
altar! He misread, however, and thought it was the lawful one ... so
he embarked on a trip to the other two, killing Death, Pestilence, and
Famine multiple times (not to mention several angels, priests,
beetles, and dragons) on the way ... only to realize that the first
place he'd been was actually where he wanted to go!

Fortunately, Krayus was both strong and stubborn, and he fought his
way all the way back across the plane, rather than succumb to the
temptation of using his helm of opposite alignment. He reached Kos's
altar, laid the amulet upon it, and was brought into demigod-hood!

